  "id": "eval.2026-09-08-reflow-152600.rag-ingestion-retrieval",
  "title": "2026-09-08-reflow-152600 · rag-ingestion-retrieval",
  "description": "# RAG ingestion and retrieval\nRead ingestion left to right across the top, then publication at right and the query flow at left. Sources carry ACLs through normalization, hash classification, version replacement, overlapping chunks and rate-limited embedding. Parse failures are isolated; embedding workers retry and retain failed inputs and attempt history in a dead-letter store.\n\nVectors, text/metadata and keyword terms must agree on version before publication. Partial writes remain unavailable for repair or rollback. Parallel vector and keyword retrieval feeds fusion and reranking, followed by user permission filtering. Sufficient authorized evidence produces an answer with citations; thin or low-scoring context produces “I don't know.” Answer feedback and unanswered questions return coverage gaps to ingestion priorities.\n\nThe lower-right rebuild flow represents background re-embedding and atomic promotion of a complete, consistent index generation. Its note specifies continued use of the current generation during rebuild and retention of the previous generation for rollback. Blue connections denote serving data and publication state; red connections mark processing failures; the dashed teal loop carries feedback.",
  "mode": "diagram",
